# Guard scripts MUST be LF. A CRLF shebang/script breaks bash silently, and a
# guard that cannot run is a guard that permits — the fail-open class that
# .claude/hooks/block-destructive-sql.sh exists to prevent.
*.sh text eol=lf
*.mjs text eol=lf

# Instruction files MUST be LF for the same reason. Claude Code parses the
# WORKING COPY, and core.autocrlf=true was writing `@AGENTS.md\r` as line 1 of
# CLAUDE.md — an import path with a trailing carriage return resolves to
# nothing, so the shared law layer would silently not load. Same failure class
# as a CRLF guard script: no error, no warning, the rules just stop applying.
CLAUDE.md text eol=lf
AGENTS.md text eol=lf

# Rendered documents are binary release artifacts. ReportLab PDFs can contain
# an ASCII-only object graph, which otherwise makes Git's whitespace checker
# misclassify valid xref records as source-code trailing whitespace.
*.pdf binary
